  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNFPA: 10 Million Safer Births Imitative (10M-SBI)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The 10 Million Safer Birth Initiative (10M-SBI) will be implemented under UNFPA&#x2019;s Maternal and New-born Health Thematic Fund (MHTF) and contribute to its overall business plan IV and its results framework, which then will support the implementation of UNFPA&#x2019;s Maternal and New-born Health and Well-Being (MNHW) Strategy.

The overall objective of the 10M-SBI is to strengthen the quality of care provided by primarily midwives as well as other sexual and reproductive health (SRH) care professionals. The 10M-SBI will promote safe and respectful SRH care practices and improve clinical knowledge and critical decision-making skills, attitudes, and competencies in a holistic, context specific, equitable and sustainable way. Partly through using the Safe Delivery App (SDA) developed by Maternity Foundation.</narrative>
  </description>
